kind: team
description: "Data platform research team — coordinator reads KB orientation, checks research-index before every task, decomposes to tool-scoped engineers (parallel dispatch), routes merged findings through platform-architect for cross-tool synthesis, then critic for claim review, and only after an all-clear dispatches to scribe for KB write-back"
topology: hub-spoke
entry_point: dp-research-coordinator
guardrail: auto

# KB: /Users/charsmith/Documents/the_vault/dp-knowledge-base/
# Orientation files every member should know about:
#   tools/_claude/research-index.md    — what's already researched (coordinator checks this first)
#   tools/_claude/cloned-repos.md      — what repos are already cloned locally
#   tools/_claude/research-workflow.md — full research + write-back protocol
#
# Flow:
#   1. coordinator reads KB orientation → checks research-index (stops if Complete)
#   2. coordinator decomposes → routes to engineer-code, engineer-catalog, engineer-docs (parallel)
#   3. engineers return CLAIMS/EVIDENCE/CONFIDENCE/OPEN QUESTIONS
#   4. platform-architect applies cross-tool synthesis lens, flags gaps
#   5. coordinator routes combined output to critic for claim review
#   6. critic issues all-clear (or returns challenged claims for resolution)
#   7. coordinator dispatches to scribe for KB write-back — never writes to KB itself

members:
  - agent: dp-research-coordinator
    role: coordinator
    description: "Read KB orientation files before every task (research-index, cloned-repos, research-workflow). If the service is already Complete in the index, tell the user and offer to answer from existing docs — do not re-research. Decompose to engineer-code, engineer-catalog, engineer-docs as needed and dispatch in parallel. After engineers return findings, route to platform-architect for cross-tool synthesis. Route the combined output to critic for claim review. Only after critic issues an all-clear dispatch to scribe for KB write-back. Never write to the KB yourself."
    context_dir: /Users/charsmith/Documents/the_vault/dp-knowledge-base/

  - agent: platform-architect
    role: specialist
    context: "Receive the merged engineer findings and apply a cross-tool synthesis lens: validate that the API surface, dependency list, and org chain tell a consistent story. Surface how the researched service fits into the broader DP topology. Flag gaps the specialist engineers missed — especially cross-tool handoffs, shared infrastructure, and governance hooks. Return structured CLAIMS/EVIDENCE/CONFIDENCE/OPEN QUESTIONS to the coordinator."
    context_dir: /Users/charsmith/Documents/the_vault/dp-knowledge-base/
    reports_to: dp-research-coordinator

  - name: engineer-code
    agent: dp-platform-engineer
    role: specialist
    context: "Source code and org focus — og (deep search, API surface, AppConfig/ConfigBin dependencies, proto/REST interface files), ta (repo activity, committer breakdown Jan–Apr), wp (org chain from top committers up to Prashanth Ramdas). Before reading any local source file: run 'git fetch && git pull' on the cloned repo and note which branch you read (include branch name in every EVIDENCE line). Cite every claim with: absolute local file path + line number + full github.netflix.net URL to the same file. Return CLAIMS/EVIDENCE/CONFIDENCE/OPEN QUESTIONS."
    reports_to: dp-research-coordinator

  - name: engineer-catalog
    agent: dp-platform-engineer
    role: specialist
    context: "Data catalog focus — cy (table metadata, schema, owner, lineage, ACL, sample data) and og for schema file references in source repos. Primary for: tables owned or consumed by a service, upstream/downstream lineage, access control groups, Iceberg/Hive metadata. Cite every cy result with the exact table name, the CLI command run, and a representative excerpt of the output. Return CLAIMS/EVIDENCE/CONFIDENCE/OPEN QUESTIONS."
    reports_to: dp-research-coordinator

  - name: engineer-docs
    agent: dp-platform-engineer
    role: specialist
    context: "Internal docs and context focus. Step 1 — check if the topic is already summarized in the KB at /Users/charsmith/Documents/the_vault/dp-knowledge-base/ (read existing overview.md/services.md before searching externally). Step 2 — fetch relevant Manuals pages and Google Docs by URL via 'ns fetch'. Step 3 — run 'ns search' for design docs, architecture RFCs, Slack threads, and team pages. Use wp for people/team lookups. Cite every claim with the exact ns URL or search result snippet used. Return CLAIMS/EVIDENCE/CONFIDENCE/OPEN QUESTIONS."
    reports_to: dp-research-coordinator

  - agent: dp-kb-scribe
    role: specialist
    context: "Only act after the coordinator confirms the critic has issued an all-clear. Write synthesized findings to tools/<service>/ following research-workflow.md exactly (frontmatter schema, overview.md/services.md/CLAUDE.md/logging.md). All written docs must link to github.netflix.net URLs — never local paths alone. Update research-index.md and cloned-repos.md if a new repo was cloned. Git commit on completion and report the commit hash back to the coordinator."
    reports_to: dp-research-coordinator

  - agent: critic
    role: specialist
    context: "Review all engineer and platform-architect findings before anything is dispatched to the scribe. Challenge any claim that: lacks a specific source (file path + line number or URL), is stated with high confidence but cited only as prior knowledge, is contradicted by other findings, or is too vague to be acted on. For each challenged claim, state the problem and the specific resolution path. Return Verified Claims, Challenged Claims with resolution paths, Gaps, and an Overall Assessment of whether findings are ready for KB write-back."
    reports_to: dp-research-coordinator
